  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two **binary** arrays AAA and BBB, of lengths NNN and MMM, respectively.\n\nYou can perform the following operation:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤min⁡(∣A∣,M)1 \\leq i \\leq \\min(|A|, M)1≤i≤min(∣A∣,M)) such that Ai=BiA_i = B_iAi​=Bi​.\n\nHere, ∣A∣|A|∣A∣ denotes the current length of AAA.\nDelete AiA_iAi​ from AAA. This reduces the length of AAA by 111.\nThen, re-index the remaining elements of AAA to start from 111, without changing their order.\nFor example, suppose A=[0,0,0,1]A = [0, 0, 0, 1]A=[0,0,0,1] and B=[1,0]B = [1, 0]B=[1,0].\n\n\nChoosing i=2i = 2i=2 (valid because A2=B2=0A_2 = B_2 = 0A2​=B2​=0) allows us to delete A2=0A_2 = 0A2​=0 from AAA.\n\nAfter this, A=[0,0,1]A = [0, 0, 1]A=[0,0,1].\nSince the elements were re-indexed, we can once again choose i=2i = 2i=2 to delete A2A_2A2​, obtaining A=[0,1]A = [0, 1]A=[0,1]. No more operations can be performed.\nFind the **minimum** possible final length of AAA, if you perform operations optimally.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the lengths of AAA and BBB.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains MMM space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BMB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_MB1​,B2​,…,BM​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible final length of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤M≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq M \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤M≤N≤3⋅105",
      "0≤Ai,Bi≤10 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 10≤Ai​,Bi​≤1",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
