      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 2\n0 0 0 1\n1 0\n4 1\n0 0 0 1\n1\n3 2\n1 0 1\n1 1",
        "output": "2\n4\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Initially, A=[0,0,0,1]A = [0, 0, 0, 1]A=[0,0,0,1] and B=[1,0]B = [1, 0]B=[1,0].\n\nChoose i=2i = 2i=2, valid because A2=B2=0A_2 = B_2 = 0A2​=B2​=0.\nAfter deletion, A=[0,0,1]A = [0, 0, 1]A=[0,0,1].\nChoose i=2i = 2i=2 again, valid because A2=B2=0A_2 = B_2 = 0A2​=B2​=0.\nAfter deletion, A=[0,1]A = [0, 1]A=[0,1].\n\nThis is the best we can do.\nTest case 222: No moves can be made at all.\nTest case 333: One optimal sequence is:\n\nChoose i=1i = 1i=1, since A1=B1=1A_1 = B_1 = 1A1​=B1​=1. After the deletion, A=[0,1]A = [0, 1]A=[0,1].\nChoose i=2i = 2i=2, since A2=B2=1A_2 = B_2 = 1A2​=B2​=1 now. After the deletion, A=[0]A = [0]A=[0].\nNo more moves can be made."
      }
